WEBVTT

00:03.960 --> 00:10.640
So now, if you compare views with cities, the cities are used in order to reduce the redundancy within

00:10.640 --> 00:12.040
one single query.

00:12.040 --> 00:15.720
So it improves the reusability within one query.

00:15.760 --> 00:21.600
Where in the other hand, in the views we are reducing the redundancies from multiple queries.

00:21.600 --> 00:24.840
So we are reducing the complexity of the whole project.

00:24.840 --> 00:29.520
So the views are improving their reusability in multiple queries.

00:29.560 --> 00:31.040
Now think about it like this.

00:31.320 --> 00:35.800
We use views in order to persist a logic in the database.

00:35.800 --> 00:40.080
So the logic is so important that we want to persist it in the database.

00:40.080 --> 00:44.760
It's like in the tables we persist data, but with the views we are persisting logic.

00:44.760 --> 00:48.640
But in the other hand in the CTE the logic is not persisted.

00:48.640 --> 00:54.840
It is temporary and can be calculated only on the fly within the scope of one query.

00:54.840 --> 01:00.880
So this logic is important only in this scenario and it is not important for any other queries.

01:00.880 --> 01:04.720
That's why it makes no sense to persist it using the views.

01:04.720 --> 01:10.400
So you have to decide is this logic is very important, then take it away from the city and put it in

01:10.400 --> 01:10.960
the view.

01:10.960 --> 01:16.400
But if you think you know what, this logic is not really important and only important in this one query.

01:16.600 --> 01:21.400
Then stay with the city, because creating views always needs some extra steps.

01:21.400 --> 01:24.840
In order to maintain the view, you have to create the view.

01:24.880 --> 01:27.080
You have to drop the view if you don't need it.

01:27.080 --> 01:29.840
But the city, there is almost no maintenance for it.

01:29.840 --> 01:35.960
The database can do automatically the cleanup once the query is done, so there is no extra activity

01:35.960 --> 01:37.960
to drop a CTE or something.

01:38.000 --> 01:41.000
That's why CTE is easier to use than views.

01:41.000 --> 01:43.960
So those are the big differences between the views and ctes.
